    "title": "Fleet Lifecycle 9.1.0.0300 Release Notes",
    "content": "<div class=\"main-content\">\n<div class=\"dita\">\n<div class=\"topic section\">\n<div class=\"topic topic concept\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en\">\n<h1 class=\"title\"><div>Fleet Lifecycle 9.1.0.0300 Release Notes</div></h1>\n<div><div class=\"p\"><div>This document contains the following sections</div></div><ul class=\"ul\"><div><li class=\"li\"><div><a class=\"xref\" data-format=\"dita\" data-scope=\"local\" data-type=\"\" href=\"https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/release-notes/patch-releases-9-1-0-x/vcf-operations/9-1-0-0300/fleet-lifecycle-9-1-0-0300-release-notes.html#GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-1de82f15-c261-4dfe-9376-486512dae608\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Introduction</a></div></li><li class=\"li\"><div><a class=\"xref\" data-format=\"dita\" data-scope=\"local\" data-type=\"\" href=\"https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/release-notes/patch-releases-9-1-0-x/vcf-operations/9-1-0-0300/fleet-lifecycle-9-1-0-0300-release-notes.html#GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-94444578-f48e-4c7f-b943-671de492fcf5\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">What's New</a></div></li><li class=\"li\"><div><a class=\"xref\" data-format=\"dita\" data-scope=\"local\" data-type=\"\" href=\"https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/release-notes/patch-releases-9-1-0-x/vcf-operations/9-1-0-0300/fleet-lifecycle-9-1-0-0300-release-notes.html#GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-9715eee1-a3a9-41ec-9def-6ff54c011a16\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Applying the Patch</a></div></li></div></ul><section class=\"section\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-1de82f15-c261-4dfe-9376-486512dae608\"><div><h2 class=\"title\"><div>Introduction</div></h2>\n<table class=\"table\">\n<div>\n<!--cq:include script=\"../../common/tablestack.jsp\" /-->\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 100.0%\"/></colgroup>\n<div>\n<tbody class=\"tbody\"><div>\n<tr class=\"row\"><div><td class=\"entry relcol\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-ae553939-f3d2-4b82-bec9-c3ec4668fcf6\"><div>\n<div class=\"p\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-c2294de9-1615-41d1-940e-a200a1b6ee1b\"><div>Fleet Lifecycle 9.1.0.0300 | 30 JUN 2026 | Build 25536195</div></div>\n<div class=\"p\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-6c9eccc5-0b24-4ef2-802f-df3d852e6038\"><div>Check for additions and updates to these release notes.</div></div>\n</div></td></div></tr>\n</div></tbody>\n</div>\n</div>\n</table>\n</div></section><section class=\"section\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-94444578-f48e-4c7f-b943-671de492fcf5\"><div><h2 class=\"title\"><div>What's New</div></h2>\n<div class=\"p\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-3ab6b87b-5301-4d64-da73-5e408194bc2d\"><div>During an upgrade from VCF 9.0.x to 9.1, after you deploy VCF management services, your existing management components are automatically added to the lifecycle inventory. If you have stale certificates, passwords, or FQDN data for a component, the automatic add might fail. Starting with version 9.1.0.0300, in the VCF Operations UI, you can see error notifications and messages that identify the components that cannot be added. In the Tasks panel, you can see warnings for all components that failed to be added and remediation guidance. For the remediation steps and instructions to add the components, see Broadcom knowledge base article <a class=\"xref\" data-format=\"html\" data-scope=\"external\" data-type=\"\" href=\"https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/441858\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">441858</a>.</div></div></div></section><section class=\"section\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-9715eee1-a3a9-41ec-9def-6ff54c011a16\"><div><h2 class=\"title\"><div>Applying the Patch</div></h2>\n<div class=\"p\" id=\"GUID-b62ea6e8-ea69-4dfc-bbdf-2cb6a5c1838a-en_id-259f17fd-592c-4229-85f6-ae55901f3455\"><div>You apply this patch by using VCF Operations. See <a class=\"xref\" data-format=\"html\" data-scope=\"external\" data-type=\"\" href=\"https://techdocs.broadcom.com/bin/gethidpage?ux-context-string=vcf_535&amp;appid=vcf-9-1&amp;language=&amp;format=rendered\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">Upgrade or Patch an Individual VCF Component</a>.</div></div></div></section></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
